WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.217 --> 00:00:01.292
Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:02.464
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.464 --> 00:00:04.984
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:07.718
will solve all of the major
problems of the world.

00:00:07.718 --> 00:00:11.631
So today's message is act despite fear.

00:00:11.631 --> 00:00:13.434
Over to you Elon Musk.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.904
(rooster crowing)

00:00:15.904 --> 00:00:18.441
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:21.331
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:25.108
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:28.155
- You are unusually fearless
and willing to go in the face

00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:29.885
of other people telling
you something is crazy.

00:00:29.885 --> 00:00:31.548
And I know a lot of pretty crazy people.

00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:32.784
You still stand out.

00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:33.710
Where does that come from, or how

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.957
do you think about making a decision

00:00:35.957 --> 00:00:37.904
when everyone tells you
this is a crazy idea?

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.800
Or where do you get the
internal strength to do that?

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.833
- Well first of all I'd say,

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:45.500
I actually think I feel
fear quite strongly,

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:48.728
so it's not as though I just have

00:00:48.728 --> 00:00:52.521
the absence of fear, I
feel it quite strongly.

00:00:52.521 --> 00:00:56.374
But there are just times when
something is important enough,

00:00:56.374 --> 00:00:58.043
that you believe in it enough,

00:00:58.043 --> 00:01:00.765
that you do it in spite of fear.

00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:02.110
- So speaking of important things.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.893
- Like people shouldn't think I ...

00:01:04.893 --> 00:01:07.261
People shouldn't think,
"I feel fear about this

00:01:07.261 --> 00:01:09.687
"and therefore I shouldn't do it."

00:01:09.687 --> 00:01:12.828
It's normal to feel
fear, like you'd have to,

00:01:12.828 --> 00:01:13.777
there'd have to be
something mentally wrong

00:01:13.777 --> 00:01:16.527
with you if you didn't feel fear.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.876
- So you just feel it
and let the importance

00:01:18.876 --> 00:01:21.099
of it drive you to do it anyway?

00:01:21.099 --> 00:01:22.807
- Yeah, actually something that

00:01:22.807 --> 00:01:26.048
can be helpful is fatalism to some degree.

00:01:26.048 --> 00:01:28.863
If you just accept the probabilities

00:01:28.863 --> 00:01:31.030
then that diminishes fear.

00:01:33.888 --> 00:01:36.332
When starting SpaceX I
thought the odds of success

00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:40.280
were less than 10%, and
I just accepted that

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.280
actually, probably I would
just lose everything,

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:47.913
but that maybe we would
make some progress.

00:01:47.913 --> 00:01:50.380
If we could just move the
ball forward, even if we died,

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.434
maybe some other company
could pick up the baton

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:57.601
and keep moving it forward so
that would still do some good.

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:00.733
Yeah, same with Tesla.

00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:02.078
I thought the odds of a car company

00:02:02.078 --> 00:02:04.408
succeeding were extremely low.

00:02:04.408 --> 00:02:06.948
- Fear is normal, it's part
of what makes you human.

00:02:06.948 --> 00:02:08.229
You would not be human, or you'd have

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:10.518
some crazy condition
if you never felt fear.

00:02:10.518 --> 00:02:12.120
I think the people who
say, "Don't be afraid,"

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.870
aren't giving you practical advice.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.286
It's, "Be afraid, feel the fear,

00:02:17.286 --> 00:02:20.189
"and then step into it and do it anyway."

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:22.133
And the more you get used to taking on

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.380
those fearful projects
that you're scared of,

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.433
the stronger you'll get, the
more resistance you'll get,

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:29.035
the higher tolerance you'll get

00:02:29.035 --> 00:02:32.250
to do bigger, better,
bolder, badder things.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.258
I think the trick though
is spotting the fear.

00:02:35.258 --> 00:02:37.313
Here's what I think
happens to most people,

00:02:37.313 --> 00:02:39.628
there's some opportunity that comes along,

00:02:39.628 --> 00:02:41.492
there's some moment that comes along,

00:02:41.492 --> 00:02:44.036
whether it's with a client,
or meeting somebody,

00:02:44.036 --> 00:02:46.201
or an event, something comes along

00:02:46.201 --> 00:02:48.506
that you're afraid of,
you're afraid of doing it,

00:02:48.506 --> 00:02:49.794
that's going to stretch you beyond

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:51.395
what you've ever done before.

00:02:51.395 --> 00:02:54.641
And then what you do is
you rationalize saying no.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:57.431
"I don't have the money
to go to that event.

00:02:57.431 --> 00:02:58.362
"I'm too busy to go out

00:02:58.362 --> 00:02:59.734
"and do that thing right now."

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.097
You find the reason why
you can't go and do it.

00:03:02.097 --> 00:03:04.947
You rationalize it, but really, deep down,

00:03:04.947 --> 00:03:07.453
the reason is you're just afraid.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.660
And until you spot the
fear, until you understand

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.929
that it's really just the fear,

00:03:12.929 --> 00:03:14.913
then you're never going
to solve the problem.

00:03:14.913 --> 00:03:18.913
So step one is understanding
when there is fear.

00:03:20.203 --> 00:03:24.114
Step two is then stepping
into it and doing it anyway,

00:03:24.114 --> 00:03:26.609
and a lot of the stuff
is just so subconscious.

00:03:26.609 --> 00:03:28.301
You know, we as human beings are kind of

00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:30.576
trained to, when we're afraid something's

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.617
going to go wrong, you have to be safe.

00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:35.313
And so it's trying to catch that

00:03:35.313 --> 00:03:38.982
subconscious action, and
proactively change it.

00:03:38.982 --> 00:03:40.671
So an example for me, when I was starting

00:03:40.671 --> 00:03:44.551
my YouTube channel, my
agent would tell me,

00:03:44.551 --> 00:03:46.432
"You have to go out and
do videos in public.

00:03:46.432 --> 00:03:47.970
"I want you to go out on the street

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.949
"and make your video in public."

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:52.306
My natural reaction

00:03:52.306 --> 00:03:55.690
was fear, but I didn't catch it.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:00.572
Initially it was, "The gear
won't be as good in public.

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:02.540
"I can't control the light settings.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.502
"I'm going to be bouncing
around with the camera.

00:04:04.502 --> 00:04:06.282
"It's not going to be a great experience

00:04:06.282 --> 00:04:08.821
"for the people watching,
why would I do that?

00:04:08.821 --> 00:04:12.472
I'm rationalizing a reason
why I don't have to do it,

00:04:12.472 --> 00:04:14.121
where really I'm just afraid.

00:04:14.121 --> 00:04:15.776
You could solve all those problems.

00:04:15.776 --> 00:04:17.860
And he told me, "Stop being afraid

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.789
"and just go out and do it."

00:04:19.789 --> 00:04:23.353
He cut through it and
let me see my own fear.

00:04:23.353 --> 00:04:25.420
And so I did it, and when I first went out

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.499
and filmed in public I
took out, it was my phone

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:28.961
or my camera, I don't remember,

00:04:28.961 --> 00:04:31.075
and I'm walking on the street,

00:04:31.075 --> 00:04:32.566
and then the postman is there.

00:04:32.566 --> 00:04:36.182
And so as soon as I see
the postman, I quiet down,

00:04:36.182 --> 00:04:39.743
I put the camera away,
just walking normally.

00:04:39.743 --> 00:04:43.582
And then when the postman
leaves, I'm back to filming.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:47.749
And that time I noticed, I'm
doing it because I'm afraid.

00:04:49.114 --> 00:04:53.992
And I got pissed, "Okay,
next time I got to speak up.

00:04:53.992 --> 00:04:55.751
"Next time I got to do better."

00:04:55.751 --> 00:04:59.536
And so I went out and forced
myself to go and do it again.

00:04:59.536 --> 00:05:00.761
And I was walking past,
and there were these

00:05:00.761 --> 00:05:02.735
construction workers, and instantly again

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:05.485
the panic sets in like,
"People are watching,

00:05:05.485 --> 00:05:06.630
"there's construction workers."

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.772
I know they don't even
really care about me

00:05:08.772 --> 00:05:11.674
and what I'm saying, what's
happening on the street.

00:05:11.674 --> 00:05:13.677
But I forced myself through it.

00:05:13.677 --> 00:05:15.283
It was awkward, it wasn't great.

00:05:15.283 --> 00:05:17.555
I think I had to redo it again anyway,

00:05:17.555 --> 00:05:20.956
but I took the step, I got better at it.

00:05:20.956 --> 00:05:23.377
I recognized the fear,
and I jumped into it,

00:05:23.377 --> 00:05:25.384
and now it's to the point
where I'll make videos

00:05:25.384 --> 00:05:26.643
walking down the hall, I'll make videos

00:05:26.643 --> 00:05:29.519
when I'm at Disneyland, Disney World.

00:05:29.519 --> 00:05:32.008
I'll make videos in the
streets of anywhere,

00:05:32.008 --> 00:05:34.291
and there's still a moment, even now,

00:05:34.291 --> 00:05:35.370
after how many videos I've done,

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.273
there's still a moment
of, "Who's watching?"

00:05:38.273 --> 00:05:39.939
I think it's natural and normal.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.726
It's not as strong as it used
to be, and more importantly,

00:05:42.726 --> 00:05:46.787
it doesn't limit me from doing
the things that I want to do.

00:05:46.787 --> 00:05:48.870
And so spotting the fear,

00:05:49.991 --> 00:05:51.860
and not rationalizing it away,

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.351
and not just doing what your
subconscious always does

00:05:54.351 --> 00:05:59.260
that keeps you down where
you are is so important.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:02.977
Being truthful that the
reason why you said no,

00:06:02.977 --> 00:06:04.376
or you're not taking this opportunity,

00:06:04.376 --> 00:06:05.844
is just because you're afraid.

00:06:05.844 --> 00:06:09.732
And the answer to saying
no should never be

00:06:09.732 --> 00:06:11.998
"Because I'm afraid."

00:06:11.998 --> 00:06:13.774
You want to re-jig your
system, so whenever

00:06:13.774 --> 00:06:16.111
that's the answer, "Because
I'm afraid to do it,"

00:06:16.111 --> 00:06:17.743
now you have to do it.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:21.123
Because you're afraid, now
you have to go out and do it.

00:06:21.123 --> 00:06:23.578
And you build your muscle to get stronger

00:06:23.578 --> 00:06:26.121
to take on new opportunities,
so you don't play safe

00:06:26.121 --> 00:06:28.490
and play small for the rest of your life.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:29.488
So the question of the day today is

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:32.483
I'm curious what's one
thing that you are afraid of

00:06:32.483 --> 00:06:36.326
or recently were afraid of
that you want to tackle?

00:06:36.326 --> 00:06:39.371
Be bold, be brave, leave it
down in the comments below.

00:06:39.371 --> 00:06:40.569
I'm really curious to find out.

00:06:40.569 --> 00:06:41.620
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.150
to Dave Lukas from Misfit Entrepreneur.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.324
Dave, thank you so much for picking up

00:06:45.324 --> 00:06:47.494
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:06:47.494 --> 00:06:48.904
I hope you enjoyed the read, man,

00:06:48.904 --> 00:06:50.879
and I really appreciate the support.

00:06:50.879 --> 00:06:52.330
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.543
I believe in you.

00:06:53.543 --> 00:06:55.488
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:55.488 --> 00:06:57.657
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:57.657 --> 00:06:59.081
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:59.081 --> 00:07:01.716
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:01.716 --> 00:07:04.352
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:07:04.352 --> 00:07:08.019
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:07:10.674 --> 00:07:11.832
- The only way to deal with fear

00:07:11.832 --> 00:07:14.107
that I found in my life, is a couple ways.

00:07:14.107 --> 00:07:17.292
One of those ways is to turn it on itself

00:07:17.292 --> 00:07:19.660
and ask yourself, "What am I afraid of?"

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.555
"I'm afraid of that?

00:07:20.555 --> 00:07:23.273
"I got to be more afraid of
what I'm going to miss out on,

00:07:23.273 --> 00:07:24.632
missing out me mission, missing out

00:07:24.632 --> 00:07:26.125
on who I'm supposed to be."

00:07:26.125 --> 00:07:27.305
In other words, if you're not

00:07:27.305 --> 00:07:29.302
getting rid of fear, then use fear.

00:07:29.302 --> 00:07:32.204
Use fear, or it uses
you, it's that simple.

00:07:32.204 --> 00:07:33.980
So you got to say, "Okay, what's the price

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.462
"if I just stay doing
this, what's the price?"

00:07:36.462 --> 00:07:38.131
I need to really, you can get scared

00:07:38.131 --> 00:07:40.558
if I learn all this, and
I don't follow through.

00:07:40.558 --> 00:07:42.661
That's something to be scared about.

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:44.123
And then that fear will get you

00:07:44.123 --> 00:07:45.899
over your fear, it'll push you through.

00:07:45.899 --> 00:07:47.442
Turn fear on itself.

00:07:47.442 --> 00:07:49.393
Second way you can do it is use

00:07:49.393 --> 00:07:50.514
what you've probably heard me say it,

00:07:50.514 --> 00:07:52.179
'cause I've used it since I was 17,

00:07:52.179 --> 00:07:54.358
is my little rocking chair test right.

00:07:54.358 --> 00:07:56.390
I'm going to sit myself
on my rocking chair,

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.257
and I'm 85 years old and
I'm looking back on my life,

00:07:59.257 --> 00:08:02.508
and I say, "I didn't
do this," or, "I did."

00:08:02.508 --> 00:08:04.008
- If there was one

00:08:05.392 --> 00:08:07.059
concept that I would

00:08:08.749 --> 00:08:11.572
suggest to people to take a daily

00:08:11.572 --> 00:08:14.072
confrontation with, it's fear.

00:08:16.539 --> 00:08:20.112
The problem with fear
is that it lies, right?

00:08:20.112 --> 00:08:22.112
So fear tells you, "Hey,

00:08:24.007 --> 00:08:26.346
"if you say that to that girl,

00:08:26.346 --> 00:08:29.277
"she's going to know she has you."

00:08:29.277 --> 00:08:31.861
"And she'll never really
be attracted to you

00:08:31.861 --> 00:08:34.301
if she knows how much
you attracted to her."

00:08:34.301 --> 00:08:35.420
(laughter)

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:36.733
"Don't say that, no."

00:08:36.733 --> 00:08:40.174
"How we get her is when
she walks by, ignore her."

00:08:40.174 --> 00:08:41.829
(laughter)

00:08:41.829 --> 00:08:44.387
- Right, it's this little
puppet on your shoulder.

00:08:44.387 --> 00:08:47.426
- Fear tells you dumb
sh-- like that, right?

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:48.381
(laughing)

00:08:48.381 --> 00:08:49.214
You know.

00:08:51.136 --> 00:08:53.636
For me the daily confrontation

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.974
with fear has become
a real practice for me

00:08:57.974 --> 00:09:01.027
since about three years ago.

00:09:01.027 --> 00:09:02.444
I went sky diving

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:08.176
in Dubai, and skydiving,
skydiving is a really

00:09:08.176 --> 00:09:10.903
interesting confront with fear, right?

00:09:10.903 --> 00:09:13.073
So I got to stand up, I'm
sorry, I got to stand up.

00:09:13.073 --> 00:09:14.554
(laughter)

00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:17.942
Alright so, all your friends, what happens

00:09:17.942 --> 00:09:19.285
you go out
- Hold this.

00:09:19.285 --> 00:09:20.780
- Oh sorry, oh, I dropped my thing.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.660
So what happens is you
go out the night before,

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.053
and, you know, you take a
drink with your friends.

00:09:26.053 --> 00:09:28.594
And somebody says, "Yeah, we
should go skydiving tomorrow!"

00:09:28.594 --> 00:09:29.881
(laughter)

00:09:29.881 --> 00:09:32.785
And you go, "Yeah, we'll go
skydiving tomorrow, yeah, yeah!"

00:09:32.785 --> 00:09:33.702
And you go, "Yeah!"

00:09:33.702 --> 00:09:36.108
And everybody goes, "Yeah."

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:38.744
And you go home, you're by
yourself, you're like, "Mm."

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:41.299
(laughter)

00:09:41.299 --> 00:09:44.208
Right, you're like "Well,
they was drunk too."

00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:45.595
(laughter)

00:09:45.595 --> 00:09:48.503
"So maybe, maybe they not, maybe ...

00:09:48.503 --> 00:09:51.474
"I mean, we don't have to
go, we don't have to do it."

00:09:51.474 --> 00:09:52.862
So then, that night, you're laying

00:09:52.862 --> 00:09:56.241
in your bed and you just keep ...

00:09:56.241 --> 00:09:58.144
And you're terrified, you keep imagining

00:09:58.144 --> 00:10:01.069
over and over again
jumping out of an airplane,

00:10:01.069 --> 00:10:04.297
and you can't figure out
why you would do that.

00:10:04.297 --> 00:10:05.192
And you're laying there, and you have

00:10:05.192 --> 00:10:07.147
the worst night's sleep of your life,

00:10:07.147 --> 00:10:08.412
but you still have the hope

00:10:08.412 --> 00:10:10.876
that your friends were drunk.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:13.668
So you wake up the next
day, and you go down,

00:10:13.668 --> 00:10:15.024
and you said where you were going to meet

00:10:15.024 --> 00:10:17.607
and everybody's there, and you're like,

00:10:17.607 --> 00:10:19.534
(laughter)

00:10:19.534 --> 00:10:22.489
"Alright, alright, cool,
cool, cool, cool, cool, cool."

00:10:22.489 --> 00:10:25.498
So you get in the van, and you don't know

00:10:25.498 --> 00:10:27.744
that your friends had the
same night that you had

00:10:27.744 --> 00:10:29.188
'cause they're pretending
like they didn't.

00:10:29.188 --> 00:10:31.417
They're like "Yeah man,
my uncle's a Navy Seal,

00:10:31.417 --> 00:10:33.534
"and, you know, this is going to be great.

00:10:33.534 --> 00:10:34.707
"I've been looking forward to this."

00:10:34.707 --> 00:10:37.088
And you like, "Oh my God, oh my God."

00:10:37.088 --> 00:10:40.142
And your stomach is terrible,
you can't eat and everything,

00:10:40.142 --> 00:10:42.125
but you don't want to be the only punk

00:10:42.125 --> 00:10:44.262
who doesn't jump out of this airplane.

00:10:44.262 --> 00:10:47.959
So you get there, and then
you have the safety brief,

00:10:47.959 --> 00:10:49.340
and you're standing there
and the guys will tell you,

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:50.563
"Well, if the chute doesn't open,

00:10:50.563 --> 00:10:51.768
what's going to happen is you do ..."

00:10:51.768 --> 00:10:53.619
"Well, why the hell, what could happen ...

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:54.918
(laughter)

00:10:54.918 --> 00:10:57.311
"That the chute wouldn't open?"

00:10:57.311 --> 00:10:58.629
So you do a thing, and what you do

00:10:58.629 --> 00:11:01.247
is your first jump
you're attached to a guy

00:11:01.247 --> 00:11:04.280
who is going to, he's going
to walk you out, so you go.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.883
And you get there, and
there's an airplane,

00:11:06.883 --> 00:11:10.396
and nobody's stopping,
everybody's still going.

00:11:10.396 --> 00:11:13.096
So you get onto the airplane,
and you're sitting there,

00:11:13.096 --> 00:11:14.648
and it's extra 'cause you're sitting

00:11:14.648 --> 00:11:16.395
on some dude's lap, some stranger.

00:11:16.395 --> 00:11:18.152
(laughter)

00:11:18.152 --> 00:11:19.832
And you're sitting on
his lap, and it's like

00:11:19.832 --> 00:11:22.129
you're trying to make
small talk, "Yeah, man."

00:11:22.129 --> 00:11:24.718
(laughter)

00:11:24.718 --> 00:11:27.121
"So you be jumping with
people all the time, huh?"

00:11:27.121 --> 00:11:28.924
(laughter)

00:11:28.924 --> 00:11:30.519
Right, you know.

00:11:30.519 --> 00:11:31.507
And then you just want to make sure,

00:11:31.507 --> 00:11:35.440
"You got kids, right, you
got people you need to see?"

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.627
You just want to make
sure he's serious, right?

00:11:36.627 --> 00:11:38.781
So you get in there,
so everything's normal.

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:41.257
So you fly and you go
up, you go up, you go up,

00:11:41.257 --> 00:11:45.332
and you go up to 14,000 feet
and you notice there's a light.

00:11:45.332 --> 00:11:48.758
It's red, and it's yellow, and green.

00:11:48.758 --> 00:11:51.405
So right now the light's red,
so then you start thinking,

00:11:51.405 --> 00:11:53.251
"At some point that
light's going to go green,"

00:11:53.251 --> 00:11:55.816
but you don't know what's going to happen.

00:11:55.816 --> 00:11:59.032
And you wait, and it goes
yellow, and the light goes green,

00:11:59.032 --> 00:12:02.069
and somebody opens the door,
and in that moment you realize

00:12:02.069 --> 00:12:05.307
you've never been in a frickin'
airplane with the door open.

00:12:05.307 --> 00:12:07.557
(laughter)

00:12:08.589 --> 00:12:10.797
Terror, oh sorry, I'm spitting, I'm sorry.

00:12:10.797 --> 00:12:12.717
(laughter)

00:12:12.717 --> 00:12:16.217
Sorry, no, terror, terror, terror, terror.

00:12:17.809 --> 00:12:19.476
So you go, and then,

00:12:20.642 --> 00:12:25.324
if you were smart you sat in
the back so you don't go first.

00:12:25.324 --> 00:12:27.756
And then people start
going out of the airplane.

00:12:27.756 --> 00:12:32.316
And you go, and the guy
walks you up to the end

00:12:32.316 --> 00:12:35.707
of the thing, and you're
standing, and your toes

00:12:35.707 --> 00:12:39.874
are on the edge, and you're
looking out down to death.

00:12:40.735 --> 00:12:42.797
(laughter)

00:12:42.797 --> 00:12:44.634
And they say, "On three!"

00:12:44.634 --> 00:12:46.669
And they say, "One, two!"

00:12:46.669 --> 00:12:49.832
And he pushes you on two
because people grab on three.

00:12:49.832 --> 00:12:52.082
(laughter)

00:12:52.946 --> 00:12:53.926
Right?

00:12:53.926 --> 00:12:55.093
And you go ...

00:12:56.297 --> 00:12:57.316
(laughter)

00:12:57.316 --> 00:13:01.648
And you fall out of the
airplane, and in one second

00:13:01.648 --> 00:13:05.529
you realize that it's the most blissful

00:13:05.529 --> 00:13:08.779
experience of your life, you're flying!

00:13:10.071 --> 00:13:12.867
It doesn't feel like falling.

00:13:12.867 --> 00:13:16.265
You actually are kind of held
a little bit by the wind,

00:13:16.265 --> 00:13:18.006
and then you start, you start falling,

00:13:18.006 --> 00:13:21.238
you falling, and there's zero fear.

00:13:21.238 --> 00:13:24.871
You realize that the
point of maximum danger

00:13:24.871 --> 00:13:27.787
is the point of minimum fear.

00:13:27.787 --> 00:13:28.704
It's bliss!

00:13:29.563 --> 00:13:30.740
It's bliss!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.716
And you're flying.

00:13:32.716 --> 00:13:34.574
(laughter)

00:13:34.574 --> 00:13:35.407
Right?

00:13:35.407 --> 00:13:36.240
And you're doing it.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:40.582
And then 20 seconds,
25 seconds, 40 seconds.

00:13:40.582 --> 00:13:42.457
And you have enough time
to just kind of be like,

00:13:42.457 --> 00:13:46.852
"Oh, shit, that's that
building I saw like that one.

00:13:46.852 --> 00:13:48.520
"Oh yeah, they see the ocean!"

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.972
(laughter)

00:13:49.972 --> 00:13:53.592
You start doing all of that,
and the lesson for me was,

00:13:53.592 --> 00:13:57.122
Why were you scared in
your bed the night before?

00:13:57.122 --> 00:13:59.681
What do you need that fear for?

00:13:59.681 --> 00:14:00.818
Just don't go.

00:14:00.818 --> 00:14:05.680
Why are you scared in your
bed 16 hours before you jump?

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.938
Why are you scared in the car?

00:14:07.938 --> 00:14:11.455
Why could you not enjoy breakfast?

00:14:11.455 --> 00:14:13.372
What did you need that?

00:14:14.523 --> 00:14:16.031
Fear of what?

00:14:16.031 --> 00:14:17.853
You're nowhere even near the airplane.

00:14:17.853 --> 00:14:20.686
Everything up to the stepping out,

00:14:21.691 --> 00:14:24.453
there's actually no reason to be scared.

00:14:24.453 --> 00:14:27.207
It only just ruins your day.

00:14:27.207 --> 00:14:29.024
You don't have to jump.

00:14:29.024 --> 00:14:31.996
And then, in that moment, all
of a sudden, where you should

00:14:31.996 --> 00:14:36.608
be terrified is the most
blissful experience of your life.

00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:40.453
And God placed the best things in life

00:14:40.453 --> 00:14:42.828
on the other side of terror.

00:14:42.828 --> 00:14:44.963
On the other side of your maximum fear

00:14:44.963 --> 00:14:47.138
are all of the best things in life.

